] [17592186316959 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,2,-4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -2{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3} \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316961 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316962 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316963 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316964 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316965 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1041 "selection" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316962 13194139534878 true] [17592186316960 1110 #uuid "80fa5116-035e-5df0-85fc-9df3ebaa4d29" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316961 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534878 true] [17592186316961 1111 #uuid "bdc19efe-e83f-535d-b7bc-269f52dfe7f8" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316962 1034 "2" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534878 true] [17592186316962 1111 #uuid "91c4e487-79de-5c11-8410-f1db1e8ce70b" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316963 1034 "1" 13194139534878 true] [17592186316963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534878 true] [17592186316963 1